# Table pagination & numbering (JobseekerModule)

Every list/table the user can browse **must** be paginated and numbered. This applies to both new tables and any existing table being substantially refactored.

## Required behavior

1. **Pagination is mandatory.** Never render an unpaginated `@for` over a server-backed (or potentially large) list.
2. **Default page size is 5.** Selectable options are **`5`, `10`, `15`**. Expose the size selector next to the pager.
3. **Row numbering is mandatory.** First column is `#`. The number is **page-aware**:
   `displayedNumber = pageIndex * pageSize + i + 1` (use `let i = $index` in the `@for`).
4. **Server-driven paging.** The page index, page size (and any `query` / `sort` filters) are passed through the **HTTP service** to the real API. Do not slice on the client when there's an API path — the API call carries the page params and the store holds the paged slice.
5. **Reset `pageIndex` to `0`** when filters, search, sort, or page size change.
6. **Footer line:** show `Showing X–Y of Z` plus the **standard pager controls** inside the bordered table shell:
   - **Per page** select (`5` / `10` / `15`)
   - **`<` / current page number (highlighted) / `>`** (not text “Prev” / “Next” buttons)
   - Disable `<` / `>` at boundaries
7. **Do not regress existing tables.** When adding a feature near a non-paginated table, paginate it as part of the same change (or note it explicitly in chat).
8. **Full list chrome** (search-on-change, filter/clear icons, table shell) — see `list-page-layout.mdc`.

## Component skeleton (signals + computed)

```ts
const PAGE_SIZE_OPTIONS = [5, 10, 15] as const;
type PageSize = (typeof PAGE_SIZE_OPTIONS)[number];

readonly pageSize = signal<PageSize>(5);
readonly pageIndex = signal(0);
readonly pageSizeOptions = PAGE_SIZE_OPTIONS;

readonly totalCount = computed(() => this.rows().length); // or from API
readonly totalPages = computed(() => Math.max(1, Math.ceil(this.totalCount() / this.pageSize())));
readonly safePageIndex = computed(() =>
  Math.min(this.pageIndex(), Math.max(0, this.totalPages() - 1))
);

readonly pagedRows = computed(() => {
  const size = this.pageSize();
  const start = this.safePageIndex() * size;
  return this.rows().slice(start, start + size); // server-paged: just `this.rows()`
});

readonly canPrev = computed(() => this.safePageIndex() > 0);
readonly canNext = computed(() => this.safePageIndex() < this.totalPages() - 1);

setPageSize(s: PageSize) { this.pageSize.set(s); this.pageIndex.set(0); /* refetch if API-paged */ }
nextPage() { if (this.canNext()) this.pageIndex.update((p) => p + 1); /* refetch if API-paged */ }
prevPage() { if (this.canPrev()) this.pageIndex.update((p) => p - 1); /* refetch if API-paged */ }
```

## Template skeleton

```html
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>#</th>
      <!-- other columns -->
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    @for (row of pagedRows(); track row.Id; let i = $index) {
      <tr>
        <td>{{ safePageIndex() * pageSize() + i + 1 }}</td>
        <!-- other cells -->
      </tr>
    }
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="…-pager">
  <span class="…-pager__summary">{{ pageFooterLabel() }}</span>
  <div class="…-pager__controls">
    <label class="…-pager__size">
      <span i18n="@@jobseeker.jobsList.perPage">Per page</span>
      <select class="form-select …-pager__select"
              [value]="pageSize()"
              (change)="setPageSize(+$any($event.target).value)">
        @for (s of pageSizeOptions; track s) { <option [value]="s">{{ s }}</option> }
      </select>
    </label>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm …-pager__nav"
            [disabled]="!canPrev()" (click)="prevPage()"
            aria-label="Prev" i18n-aria-label="@@jobseeker.common.prev">&lt;</button>
    <span class="…-pager__page …-pager__page--active">{{ safePageIndex() + 1 }}</span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm …-pager__nav"
            [disabled]="!canNext()" (click)="nextPage()"
            aria-label="Next" i18n-aria-label="@@jobseeker.common.next">&gt;</button>
  </div>
</div>
```

Copy pager bar styles from an existing list (e.g. `.aer-pager` / `.dmv-pager` / `.ia-pager`): tinted footer strip, active page pill.
## API + NgRx wiring (server-paged)

- The HTTP service method takes `pageIndex` / `pageSize` (+ filters) and returns `{ rows, total }`.
- Mock interceptor honors the same params (slice the in-memory list and return `total`).
- After a successful response, dispatch into the slice (e.g. `cacheRows({ rows, total, pageIndex, pageSize })`); the table reads from selectors.
- Refetch on **page change**, **size change**, **search/filter/sort change**, and after **mutations** that affect the list. See `http-store-sync.mdc`.

## Bilingual labels

Use `$localize` / `i18n` for "Prev", "Next", "Showing X–Y of Z", "Per page", and the `#` header tooltip if any. Keep the matching `messages.ar.json` entries in sync.
